ARC Upgrade Readiness Assessment

Upgrade path: 0.14.2 → 0.15.0

🔴 NO-GO — Blockers must be resolved before upgrading

Inventory

Component	Resource	Namespace	Chart	Image	Container Mode
Controller	arc-gha-rs-controller	arc-systems	gha-rs-controller-0.14.2	ghcr.io/actions/gha-runner-scale-set-controller:0.14.2	—
Scale Set	arc-runner-set	arc-runners	gha-rs-0.14.2	ghcr.io/actions/actions-runner:**latest**	Kubernetes (pod-mode)
🚨 Blockers — Must fix before upgrade

1. CRDs must be applied manually first

All 4 CRDs have changed in 0.15.0. Helm does not upgrade CRDs automatically. If you run helm upgrade without pre-applying the new CRDs, the controller will run against stale API schemas and behaviour is undefined.

CRD	Status
autoscalinglisteners.actions.github.com	⚠️ Changed
autoscalingrunnersets.actions.github.com	⚠️ Changed
ephemeralrunners.actions.github.com	⚠️ Changed
ephemeralrunnersets.actions.github.com	⚠️ Changed
Required action — apply CRDs from the 0.15.0 chart bundle before running helm upgrade:

helm show crds \
  oci://ghcr.io/actions/actions-runner-controller-charts/gha-rs-controller \
  --version 0.15.0 | kubectl apply -f -

⚠️ Fix Before Upgrade

2. Runner image pinned to latest — unacceptable for production

arc-runner-set uses ghcr.io/actions/actions-runner:latest. This is a floating tag — you cannot know what version is running, rollback is impossible, and the image may silently change between pod restarts. The current latest actions/runner release is v2.338.0.

Required action — pin the runner image in your scale set values.yaml:

template:
  spec:
    containers:
      - name: runner
        image: ghcr.io/actions/actions-runner:2.338.0

3. Runner image is outdated (relative to latest runner release)

Even if pinned today, the latest tag resolves to an image that is almost certainly behind the current runner release v2.338.0. The release notes for 0.15.0 bundle runner v2.337.0 internally; anything older has known bugs fixed in later releases.

ℹ️ Warnings

4. Notable behavioral changes in 0.15.0 to be aware of

The 0.15.0 release is a significant internal refactor. Key changes that may affect your environment:

Area	Change
Reconciliation model	Resources are now upgraded in-place (1-1 mapping between AutoscalingRunnerSet and EphemeralRunnerSet). The actions.github.com/change-hash annotation is removed in favour of metadata.generation tracking.
Status fields removed	AutoscalingRunnerSet printer columns for pendingRunners, runningRunners, finishedRunners, deletingRunners are removed — replaced by metrics. Any dashboards or scripts reading these fields will break.
Listener drift detection	Listener pod is now replaced by comparing the pod spec directly (not a hash). Expect a one-time listener pod restart on first upgrade.
--default-max-concurrent-reconciles flag removed	If you pass this flag in your controller values.yaml → args, the controller will fail to start. The flag is replaced by per-controller settings.
Outdated runner lifecycle	Runners in an Outdated phase now cause the scale set to switch off (drain) rather than rebuild immediately. This changes draining behaviour during rolling upgrades.
Metadata validation	Chart now rejects integer values in labels/annotations at render time (helm upgrade will error out if any are present).
Scale-set re-registration	Scale sets that disappear from the Actions service are now automatically re-registered — no manual intervention needed.
Secret deletion handling	Deleting the githubConfigSecret now cleanly releases the AutoscalingRunnerSet finalizer.
5. Zero active EphemeralRunners — good timing

✅ There are 0 running EphemeralRunners across all scale sets. This is the ideal window to upgrade with no in-flight job disruption.

Upgrade-Day Sequence

Complete all Blockers and Fix Before Upgrade items first.

Step 1 — Verify no jobs are running (already confirmed: 0 EphemeralRunners)
         kubectl get ephemeralrunners -A

Step 2 — Apply updated CRDs from the 0.15.0 chart
         helm show crds \
           oci://ghcr.io/actions/actions-runner-controller-charts/gha-rs-controller \
           --version 0.15.0 | kubectl apply -f -

Step 3 — Upgrade the controller (namespace: arc-systems, release: arc)
         helm upgrade arc \
           oci://ghcr.io/actions/actions-runner-controller-charts/gha-rs-controller \
           --version 0.15.0 \
           --namespace arc-systems \
           --reuse-values

         # Verify controller is healthy
         kubectl rollout status deployment/arc-gha-rs-controller -n arc-systems

Step 4 — Upgrade scale set: arc-runner-set (namespace: arc-runners)
         # Ensure your values.yaml pins the runner image to 2.338.0 first!
         helm upgrade arc-runner-set \
           oci://ghcr.io/actions/actions-runner-controller-charts/gha-rs-runner-scale-set \
           --version 0.15.0 \
           --namespace arc-runners \
           --reuse-values \
           --set template.spec.containers[0].image=ghcr.io/actions/actions-runner:2.338.0

Step 5 — Confirm scale set phase is Running
         kubectl get autoscalingrunnerset arc-runner-set -n arc-runners

Step 6 — Update any dashboards/alerts that read status sub-fields
         (pendingRunners, runningRunners, etc.) — switch them to metrics.
Summary

#	Finding	Severity
1	All 4 CRDs changed — must kubectl apply before helm upgrade	🔴 Blocker
2	Runner image uses floating latest tag	🟠 Fix before upgrade
3	Runner image likely behind latest v2.338.0	🟠 Fix before upgrade
4	--default-max-concurrent-reconciles flag removed in 0.15.0	🟠 Check your values
5	Status printer columns removed — dashboards may break	🟡 Warning
6	Large internal reconciliation refactor — validate in staging first	🟡 Warning
7	0 running EphemeralRunners — ideal upgrade window	✅ Good



