# ARC Upgrade Readiness Assessment

**Upgrade path:** `0.14.2` → `0.15.0`
**Verdict:** 🔴 NO-GO — Blockers must be resolved before upgrading

---

## Inventory

| Component | Resource | Namespace | Chart | Image | Container Mode |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| **Controller** | `arc-gha-rs-controller` | `arc-systems` | `gha-rs-controller-0.14.2` | `ghcr.io/actions/gha-runner-scale-set-controller:0.14.2` | — |
| **Scale Set** | `arc-runner-set` | `arc-runners` | `gha-rs-0.14.2` | `ghcr.io/actions/actions-runner:latest` | Kubernetes (pod-mode) |

---

## 🚨 Blockers — Must fix before upgrade

### 1. CRDs must be applied manually first

All **4 CRDs** have changed in 0.15.0. Helm does **not** upgrade CRDs
automatically. Running `helm upgrade` without pre-applying the new CRDs will
leave the controller running against stale API schemas.

| CRD | Status |
|---|---|
| `autoscalinglisteners.actions.github.com` | ⚠️ Changed |
| `autoscalingrunnersets.actions.github.com` | ⚠️ Changed |
| `ephemeralrunners.actions.github.com` | ⚠️ Changed |
| `ephemeralrunnersets.actions.github.com` | ⚠️ Changed |

Apply CRDs from the 0.15.0 chart bundle **before** running `helm upgrade`:

```bash
helm show crds \
  oci://ghcr.io/actions/actions-runner-controller-charts/gha-rs-controller \
  --version 0.15.0 | kubectl apply -f -

🟠 Fix Before Upgrade

2. Runner image pinned to latest — unacceptable for production

arc-runner-set uses ghcr.io/actions/actions-runner:latest. This is a floating tag — the running version is unknown, rollback is impossible, and the image may silently change between pod restarts.
The current latest actions/runner release is v2.338.0.

Pin the runner image in your scale set values.yaml:

template:
  spec:
    containers:
      - name: runner
        image: ghcr.io/actions/actions-runner:2.338.0

3. Runner image is outdated relative to latest runner release

The latest tag almost certainly resolves to a runner older than v2.338.0. The 0.15.0 chart bundles runner v2.337.0 internally; anything older carries known bugs fixed in later releases.

4. --default-max-concurrent-reconciles flag removed in 0.15.0

If this flag is present in your controller values.yaml under args, the controller pod will fail to start after upgrade. It has been replaced by per-controller settings.

Check your current args:

kubectl get deployment arc-gha-rs-controller -n arc-systems \
  -o jsonpath='{.spec.template.spec.containers[0].args}'

Remove --default-max-concurrent-reconciles from your values.yaml before upgrading.

🟡 Warnings

5. Significant behavioral changes in 0.15.0

Area	Change
Reconciliation model	Resources upgraded in-place (1-1 mapping between AutoscalingRunnerSet and EphemeralRunnerSet). The actions.github.com/change-hash annotation is removed; tracking now uses metadata.generation.
Status fields removed	AutoscalingRunnerSet printer columns pendingRunners, runningRunners, finishedRunners, deletingRunners are removed — replaced by metrics. Dashboards or scripts reading these fields will break.
Listener drift detection	Listener pod is now replaced by comparing the pod spec directly (not a hash). Expect a one-time listener pod restart on first upgrade.
Outdated runner lifecycle	Runners in an Outdated phase now cause the scale set to switch off (drain) rather than rebuild immediately. This changes draining behaviour during rolling upgrades.
Metadata validation	Chart now rejects integer values in labels/annotations at render time. helm upgrade will error if any are present.
Scale-set re-registration	Scale sets that disappear from the Actions service are now automatically re-registered — no manual intervention needed.
Secret deletion handling	Deleting the githubConfigSecret now cleanly releases the AutoscalingRunnerSet finalizer.
6. Validate in staging first

The 0.15.0 release is a large internal reconciliation refactor. Run it in a non-production environment before rolling to production.

✅ 7. Zero active EphemeralRunners — good upgrade window

There are 0 running EphemeralRunners across all scale sets. This is the ideal time to upgrade with no in-flight job disruption.

Upgrade-Day Sequence

Complete all Blockers and Fix Before Upgrade items first.

# Step 1 — Confirm no jobs are running
kubectl get ephemeralrunners -A

# Step 2 — Apply updated CRDs from the 0.15.0 chart
helm show crds \
  oci://ghcr.io/actions/actions-runner-controller-charts/gha-rs-controller \
  --version 0.15.0 | kubectl apply -f -

# Step 3 — Upgrade the controller (release: arc, namespace: arc-systems)
helm upgrade arc \
  oci://ghcr.io/actions/actions-runner-controller-charts/gha-rs-controller \
  --version 0.15.0 \
  --namespace arc-systems \
  --reuse-values

# Verify controller is healthy
kubectl rollout status deployment/arc-gha-rs-controller -n arc-systems

# Step 4 — Upgrade scale set: arc-runner-set (namespace: arc-runners)
#           Ensure runner image is pinned in values.yaml before this step.
helm upgrade arc-runner-set \
  oci://ghcr.io/actions/actions-runner-controller-charts/gha-rs-runner-scale-set \
  --version 0.15.0 \
  --namespace arc-runners \
  --reuse-values \
  --set template.spec.containers[0].image=ghcr.io/actions/actions-runner:2.338.0

# Step 5 — Confirm scale set phase is Running
kubectl get autoscalingrunnerset arc-runner-set -n arc-runners

# Step 6 — Update dashboards/alerts that read status sub-fields
#           (pendingRunners, runningRunners, etc.) — migrate them to metrics.

Summary

#	Finding	Severity
1	All 4 CRDs changed — must kubectl apply before helm upgrade	🔴 Blocker
2	Runner image uses floating latest tag	🟠 Fix before upgrade
3	Runner image likely behind latest v2.338.0	🟠 Fix before upgrade
4	--default-max-concurrent-reconciles flag removed in 0.15.0	🟠 Fix before upgrade
5	Status printer columns removed — dashboards may break	🟡 Warning
6	Large internal reconciliation refactor — validate in staging first	🟡 Warning
7	0 running EphemeralRunners — ideal upgrade window	✅ Good



